  "headline": "The City of Lakes",
  "short_description": "Udaipur's palaces rise from the waters of Lake Pichola, earning it a reputation as one of India's most romantic cities.",
  "about": "Founded in 1559 by Maharana Udai Singh II, Udaipur is known for its lakes, palaces and Mewar Rajput heritage.\n\nLocated in the Aravalli hills of southern Rajasthan, around Lake Pichola and Fateh Sagar Lake.\n\nKnown for Mewar-school miniature paintings, puppetry (kathputli) and lakeside havelis.\n\nPredominantly Hindu, with the Jagdish Temple as a major shrine in the old city.",
  "history": "Capital of the Mewar Kingdom after the fall of Chittorgarh, ruled by a dynasty tracing its lineage over a thousand years.",
  "history_verified": false,
  "transportation": "- Maharana Pratap Airport (airport)\n- Udaipur City Railway Station (railway)\n- Udaipur Bus Stand (bus terminal)",
  "travel_info": "Languages: Hindi, Rajasthani, English\nBudget: premium",
  "best_time_text": "September to March",
  "ideal_duration_text": "2–3 days",
  "nearest_airport": "Maharana Pratap Airport (UDR)",
